{"kind":"assert","text":"Ruling on d9cc0f52: no workflow edit in BR-13. One more Card\nattempt, later, then a named fallback.\n\nThe Page workflow has the same install step, byte for byte, and its\nrun 42761381020 passed that step beside the two Card timeouts. The\nstep is sound. The Azure package mirror failed for two runners.\nThat is an outage outside the repository, and a mirror edit would\nput a workflow change into a head that is about version questions.\n\n1. Rerun the failed Card job once more on unchanged a591, no\n   earlier than 02:00 EST. The attempt does not wait for the local\n   gate and the gate does not wait for it. Keep the workflow, the\n   pins and the 15-minute limit.\n2. If that attempt runs the three browser witnesses, its result is\n   BR-13's Card evidence.\n3. If it is cancelled again at the install step, stop the retries.\n   Send BR-13 to review with these facts in the note: Card run\n   42757844594 passed at fb98fb2e, the exact diff from fb98fb2e to\n   the reviewed head (the Counter and Lending test alias maps, the\n   Counter browser alias and notes), and the three cancelled\n   attempts with their annotations. The checker decides whether\n   that carries. The Card workflow runs again on main after the\n   landing, and a failed witness there blocks the next head.\n4. A mirror change is a separate small head, and I file it only if\n   the install step still fails after 09:00 EST. It then applies to\n   both browser workflows, which share the step.\n\nSequence: the sampled gate at ff0eee7d runs when it is ready. It\nneeds nothing from this ruling.\n\nI read your abort report 4840f7da: workerd exited, the owner at the\nabort is unknown. That is enough for the sampled gate.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}